; Harrison's sources, one module per chapter topic.  Each module opens the
; ones it actually depends on.
;
; -open Format -open Num -open Str replaces the opens initialization.ml used
; to contribute to every file back when the sources were concatenated into a
; single compilation unit.  The order matters: Str and Num deliberately
; shadow parts of Format.
;
; The warning profile is "all, minus what the book's style trips everywhere":
;   -4   fragile-match          331 sites
;   -27  unused-var-strict      373 sites
;   -32..70 as a block, then 32, 33, 39, 41, 52 and 56 put back
; What that leaves off is mainly 44/45 (open-shadow-identifier, inherent to
; the open chain) and 70 (missing-mli, there are no .mli files).
;
; Everything else is on, including 8 (partial-match).  The 26 files that
; still trip something carry a file-local [@@@warning "-N"] instead, written
; by tools/localize_warnings.py, so the other 16 keep the full check.
;
; -warn-error -a keeps warnings from failing the build on compiler versions
; that add new ones.  -no-strict-sequence is required because dune enables
; -strict-sequence by default, which rejects lib.ml's
; "let can f x = try f x; true with ...".
(library
 (name atp)
 (libraries num str)
 (flags
  (:standard
   -w
   +a-4-27-32..70+32+33+39+41+52+56
   -warn-error
   -a
   -no-strict-sequence
   -open Format
   -open Num
   -open Str))
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_atp_quot)))
